<title>NETHERLANDS: VAN LEER SIGNS DEAL WITH BAYER.</title>
<headline>VAN LEER SIGNS DEAL WITH BAYER.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-01-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dutch packaging group Van Leer said on Thursday it had signed a contract with German chemical firm Bayer for the delivery of steel and fibre barrels.</p>
<p>&quot;Van Leer will start delivering steel barrels to Bayer units in the U.S., South America, Europe and Singapore,&quot; it said.</p>
<p>Fibre barrels will only be delivered to Bayer units in Europe.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000</p>
